            "text": "Feature\nDiscrete Probability \nDistribution\nContinuous Probability Distribution",
            "block_type": 0
          },
          {
            "bbox": [
              12.0,
              82.64,
              95.03,
              102.71
            ],
            "text": "Definition",
            "block_type": 0
          },
          {
            "bbox": [
              132.53,
              60.99,
              354.48,
              124.31
            ],
            "text": "Describes the probability of \noutcomes that can take on \ncountable distinct values.",
            "block_type": 0
          },
          {
            "bbox": [
              12.0,
              60.99,
              701.13,
              170.99
            ],
            "text": "Describes the probability of outcomes \nthat can take on any value within a \ncontinuous range or interval.\nPossible \nValues",
            "block_type": 0
          },
          {
            "bbox": [
              132.53,
              129.32,
              387.57,
              170.99
            ],
            "text": "Finite or countably infinite (e.g., \n0, 1, 2, 3...)",
            "block_type": 0
          },
          {
            "bbox": [
              396.22,
              129.32,
              673.14,
              170.99
            ],
            "text": "Uncountably infinite (e.g., any real \nnumber between a and b)",
            "block_type": 0
          },
          {
