      "kind": "page_text",
      "text": "Continuous Distributions\n\nContinuous random variables may assume an infinite number of values\nover a finite or infinite range. The probability distribution of a\ncontinuous random variable X is often called the probability density\nfunction f(x). The total area under the probability density function is 1.\n\nNormal Distribution\n\nThe most widely used distribution in the theory of statistical quality\ncontrol is the normal distribution. The probability density function of a\nnormal random variable is given by\n                 1     𝑓𝑥=    𝑒𝑥𝑝−𝑥−𝜇2   , −∞< 𝑥< ∞\n                           2𝜎2                2𝜋𝜎\n\nWhere μ is the population mean and σ is the population standard\ndeviation.\n\n\n\n\n                                        ME3327E QUALITY, RELIABILITY AND",
